<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:34px 0 12px;font:600 11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680"><span style="padding:3px 7px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff;border-radius:4px">01b</span><span style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:#1c1b19">First run — nothing in specs/ yet</span></div>
<div style="width:760px;background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">
<div style="font:600 15px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;margin-bottom:16px">Ahoy</div>
<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:34px 32px;max-width:560px">
<div style="font:600 17px/1.3 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;margin-bottom:8px">No stories here yet.</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#3f3d39;font-size:13.5px;max-width:52ch;text-wrap:pretty">Give Ahoy the key of a Jira ticket that already exists and it will fetch it, plan the work, and stop for you to read the plan. Nothing is created in Jira.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;color:#8a8680;font-size:12.5px">Watching <span style="font:12px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862">specs/</span> — the directory is readable and empty.</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center">
<input value="R3DA-" style="width:190px;padding:9px 12px;border:1px solid #c9d8f7;border-radius:8px;font:13px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#1c1b19;outline:2px solid #dbe6fd" />
<button style="padding:10px 16px;background:#2563eb;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Start</button>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<sc-if value="{{ showNotes }}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
<div style="flex:none;width:320px;position:sticky;top:16px;font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="border-left:2px solid #cfcbc4;padding:2px 0 2px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:6px">BRIEF 1 · TRIAGE</div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Three signals, not one. <b>Which group</b> answers "does it want me". <b>The third line</b> answers "is it moving" in words, not a badge — <i>output 3s ago</i>, <i>nothing running since 11:02</i>. <b>Left edge colour</b> is redundant with both, so colour-blindness costs nothing.</p></div>
<div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#fbf1dd;color:#8a5a00;font:600 10px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em">BEHAVIOUR CHANGE</span><p style="margin:6px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty">Stalled becomes its own group with its own words — "stopped moving" rather than a phase badge — because <i>implementation</i> looks identical whether a process is alive or the laptop was shut. This is derived from state.json's last-write time plus whether a router pid is alive; the browser still decides nothing.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>The detail pane on home is a work queue, not a dashboard.</b> Only the stories that want a decision get a card and a verb; everything else is a quiet table. There is no summary tile, no chart, no count-up — the number in the header is the only aggregate that changes behaviour.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>Last moved</b> is an absolute time plus an elapsed one. Elapsed alone re-renders every poll and reads as motion where there is none.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>Unreadable directory</b> sits in the list, at the bottom, in the story-shaped place a story would be — a directory that cannot be parsed is a story you are not seeing, and hiding it in a toast would be a lie of omission. It links to the verbatim script output (artboard <a href="#a10">10</a>).</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>Empty state</b> puts the input in the page, not behind a button: on first run there is exactly one thing to do. It also states the one thing people get wrong — Ahoy never creates the ticket.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</sc-if>
</div>

<div id="a2" style="padding:24px 48px 12px;display:flex;gap:34px;align-items:flex-start;scroll-margin-top:16px">
<div style="flex:none;width:1180px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:0 0 12px;font:600 11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680"><span style="padding:3px 7px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff;border-radius:4px">02</span><span style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:#1c1b19">New story — one box, one verb, four states</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-start;font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">

<div style="flex:none;width:274px">
<div style="font:11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:8px">collapsed</div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:12px">
<button style="width:100%;text-align:left;padding:10px 12px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;cursor:pointer">+ New story</button>
</div>
</div>

<div style="flex:none;width:274px">
<div style="font:11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:8px">open</div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:12px">
<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px">
<input value="R3DA-14022" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:9px 11px;border:1px solid #2563eb;border-radius:8px;font:13px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#1c1b19;outline:3px solid #dbe6fd" />
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:10px">
<button style="flex:1;padding:9px 0;background:#2563eb;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Start</button>
<button style="flex:1;padding:9px 0;background:#fff;color:#3f3d39;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Cancel</button>
</div>
<p style="margin:11px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6862;text-wrap:pretty">The key of a ticket that already exists. This creates the story here, never in Jira.</p>
<p style="margin:7px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.45;color:#6b6862">Already have <span style="font:11.5px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">R3DA-14022</span>? The same box picks it back up.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="flex:none;width:274px">
<div style="font:11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:8px">key not recognised</div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:12px">
<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px">
<input value="r3da 14o22" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:9px 11px;border:1px solid #d98b82;border-radius:8px;font:13px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#1c1b19;background:#fffbfa" />
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:10px">
<button style="flex:1;padding:9px 0;background:#f0eeea;color:#a5a099;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Start</button>
<button style="flex:1;padding:9px 0;background:#fff;color:#3f3d39;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Cancel</button>
</div>
<p style="margin:11px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.45;color:#b4261a;text-wrap:pretty">That isn't the shape of a Jira key. Ahoy expects letters, a hyphen, then digits — like <span style="font:11.5px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">R3DA-14022</span>. Nothing has been run.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="flex:none;width:300px">
<div style="font:11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:8px">the script refused</div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:12px">
<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px">
<input value="R3DA-99999" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:9px 11px;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:13px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862" />
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:10px">
<button style="flex:1;padding:9px 0;background:#2563eb;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Try again</button>
<button style="flex:1;padding:9px 0;background:#fff;color:#3f3d39;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Cancel</button>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:11px;border:1px solid #f2cdc8;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden">
<div style="background:#fdf6f5;padding:9px 11px;border-bottom:1px solid #f2cdc8">
<div style="font:600 12px/1.35 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#b4261a">The harness refused. No story was created.</div>
<div style="font:11px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a5a00;margin-top:3px">bin/run.sh R3DA-99999 → exit 4</div>
</div>
<pre style="margin:0;padding:9px 11px;background:#1c1b19;color:#e6e2db;font:11px/1.55 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;max-height:96px;overflow:auto">jira: issue R3DA-99999 not found
(or the token cannot see it)</pre>
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;padding:8px 11px;background:#fff"><button style="padding:5px 9px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:6px;font:11.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39;cursor:pointer">Copy output</button></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<sc-if value="{{ showNotes }}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
<div style="flex:none;width:320px;position:sticky;top:16px;font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="border-left:2px solid #cfcbc4;padding:2px 0 2px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:6px">ONE BOX, ONE VERB</div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Start and resume stay a single field. The helper text says the resume behaviour out loud rather than adding a second control for it — a second control implies a choice the user does not have to make.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>Client-side validation only says "this is not a key".</b> It never says "this ticket does not exist" — the browser cannot know that, and a UI that guesses at the harness's answer is exactly the class of bug we are avoiding. Start is unarmed, and the copy states that nothing ran.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>Refusal shows three things in order:</b> what it means in a sentence, the command and exit code, then stderr verbatim in a scrolling block. Never a paraphrase of stderr — if we cannot show it faithfully we show it raw.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The refusal block replaces the panel's own body rather than appearing as a toast, so a 3-second redraw cannot destroy it and the half-typed key survives beside it.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</sc-if>
</div>

<div id="a3" style="padding:24px 48px 12px;display:flex;gap:34px;align-items:flex-start;scroll-margin-top:16px">
<div style="flex:none;width:1180px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:0 0 12px;font:600 11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680"><span style="padding:3px 7px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff;border-radius:4px">03</span><span style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:#1c1b19">Agent running — nothing is being asked of you</span></div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px 20px;font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:14px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px"><span style="font:600 20px/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:-.01em">R3DA-14022</span><span style="font-size:13.5px;color:#6b6862">Description column in picker · frontend</span></div>
<a href="#" style="font-size:12.5px;text-decoration:none">Jira ↗</a>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px;margin-bottom:6px">
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#e8f4ec;color:#157f4a;font:500 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">intake</span>
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#157f4a;color:#fff;font:600 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">planning</span>
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#f0eeea;color:#a5a099;font:500 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">◆ plan review</span>
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#f0eeea;color:#a5a099;font:500 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">implementation</span>
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#f0eeea;color:#a5a099;font:500 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">pr review</span>
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#f0eeea;color:#a5a099;font:500 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">◆ delivery gate</span>
<span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;background:#f0eeea;color:#a5a099;font:500 12px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">done</span>
</div>
<div style="font-size:12px;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:16px">◆ marks the two phases only a human can move.</div>

<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #e8e5e0;background:#f7fbf8">
<span style="width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;background:#157f4a;flex:none"></span>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font:600 13.5px/1.3 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#157f4a">Cartographer is working</div>
<div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#3f3d39;margin-top:2px">It printed something 2 seconds ago. Nothing is being asked of you — you can close this tab.</div>
</div>
<div style="font:11.5px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;text-align:right;flex:none">pid 48210 · 6m 12s<br /><span style="color:#a5a099">planning</span></div>
<button style="flex:none;padding:7px 12px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:500 12.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39;cursor:pointer">Stop the run</button>
</div>
<pre style="margin:0;padding:16px 18px;background:#1c1b19;color:#d8d4cc;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;height:250px;overflow:auto">  reading specs/R3DA-14022/jira-source.md
  ticket parsed: 1 description block, 3 comments
<span style="color:#8fb9a0">✓</span> derived 5 candidate acceptance criteria
  mapping criteria to repositories
    frontend        AC1 AC2 AC4 AC5
    all-facilities  AC1 AC4 AC5
  checking that every criterion quotes the ticket
<span style="color:#8fb9a0">✓</span> 5 of 5 criteria carry a source quote
  drafting work packages
    WP1  column picker · frontend
    WP2  description column plumbing · all-facilities
  estimating test ids for WP1<span style="background:#d8d4cc;color:#1c1b19"> </span></pre>
<div style="padding:12px 16px;border-top:1px solid #e8e5e0;background:#fff">
<div style="display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-end">
<textarea placeholder="Type here if you want to interrupt — nothing is sent until you press Send." style="flex:1;height:38px;box-sizing:border-box;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:13px/1.3 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;resize:none;background:#faf9f7"></textarea>
<button style="flex:none;padding:10px 16px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39;cursor:pointer">Send</button>
</div>
<div style="font-size:12px;color:#8a8680;margin-top:8px">The agent has not paused. Anything you send goes to the terminal whenever it next reads input.</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<sc-if value="{{ showNotes }}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
<div style="flex:none;width:320px;position:sticky;top:16px;font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="border-left:2px solid #cfcbc4;padding:2px 0 2px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:6px">BRIEF 2 · THE LIVE CONVERSATION</div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The transcript stays raw and monospace — it is the truth, and dressing it as chat bubbles would invent structure the stream does not have. What changes is the <b>strip above it</b>, which is the only part that makes a claim, and states its evidence: "printed something 2 seconds ago".</p></div>
<div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#fbf1dd;color:#8a5a00;font:600 10px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em">BEHAVIOUR CHANGE</span><p style="margin:6px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty">The reply box is <b>always present and always enabled</b>. Today it is armed by the 3-second inference, which means the inference can lock you out of a terminal that really is waiting. Typing into a pty that isn't reading costs nothing; being unable to type costs the story. The inference now only changes the <i>hint</i>, never the ability.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">"You can close this tab" is doing real work: this user starts a story and leaves. Saying so removes the pull to sit and watch.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>pid and elapsed time</b> are the honest answer to "is this actually alive", and they are what distinguishes this screen from artboard <a href="#a10">10</a>'s stalled state.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The dark transcript is the one non-light surface in the product. It is a terminal; pretending otherwise makes the ANSI colours the agent emits look like a bug.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</sc-if>
</div>

<div id="a4" style="padding:24px 48px 12px;display:flex;gap:34px;align-items:flex-start;scroll-margin-top:16px">
<div style="flex:none;width:1180px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:0 0 12px;font:600 11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680"><span style="padding:3px 7px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff;border-radius:4px">04</span><span style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:#1c1b19">Agent waiting — Cartographer appears to have asked something</span></div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px 20px;font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:16px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px"><span style="font:600 20px/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:-.01em">R3DA-14022</span><span style="font-size:13.5px;color:#6b6862">Description column in picker · frontend</span></div>
<a href="#" style="font-size:12.5px;text-decoration:none">Jira ↗</a>
</div>
<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8c98a;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 0 0 3px #fbf1dd">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px;padding:14px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #e8c98a;background:#fdfaf2">
<span style="width:9px;height:9px;background:#c98a00;flex:none;margin-top:5px"></span>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font:600 13.5px/1.3 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#8a5a00">Quiet for 14 seconds — it looks like it is waiting for you</div>
<div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#3f3d39;margin-top:3px;max-width:78ch;text-wrap:pretty">Ahoy cannot see whether the agent is reading input. It has printed nothing since 11:24:06 and its last line ends in a question mark, so this is a guess — a good one, but a guess.</div>
</div>
<div style="font:11.5px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;text-align:right;flex:none">pid 48210 · alive<br /><span style="color:#a5a099">planning</span></div>
</div>
<div style="padding:16px 18px;background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid #e8e5e0">
<div style="font:600 10px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:8px">THE LAST THING IT PRINTED</div>
<div style="font:14px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#1c1b19;background:#faf9f7;border-left:3px solid #c98a00;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;text-wrap:pretty">AC2 says re-ordering is "optional". Do you want it planned as a<br />work package now, or dropped from scope and left in the ticket? [order/drop]</div>
</div>
<pre style="margin:0;padding:16px 18px;background:#1c1b19;color:#d8d4cc;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;height:170px;overflow:auto">    WP1  column picker · frontend
    WP2  description column plumbing · all-facilities
  estimating test ids for WP1
<span style="color:#8fb9a0">✓</span> WP1 → 4 test ids
  AC2 is marked optional in the source quote
<span style="color:#e0b878">?</span> AC2 says re-ordering is "optional". Do you want it planned as a
  work package now, or dropped from scope and left in the ticket? [order/drop]
<span style="background:#d8d4cc;color:#1c1b19"> </span></pre>
<div style="padding:14px 16px;border-top:1px solid #e8e5e0;background:#fdfaf2">
<div style="display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-end">
<textarea style="flex:1;height:66px;box-sizing:border-box;padding:11px 13px;border:1px solid #c98a00;border-radius:8px;font:13.5px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;resize:none;background:#fff;outline:3px solid #fbf1dd">order — but put it last, behind the description column.</textarea>
<button style="flex:none;padding:11px 18px;background:#2563eb;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:500 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Send</button>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;color:#8a5a00">
<span>Sent to the terminal as typed, with a newline. Nothing is interpreted on the way.</span>
<span style="color:#8a8680;font:11.5px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">draft kept through refresh</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<sc-if value="{{ showNotes }}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
<div style="flex:none;width:320px;position:sticky;top:16px;font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="border-left:2px solid #cfcbc4;padding:2px 0 2px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:6px">HOW TO BE UNCERTAIN OUT LOUD</div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Three levels of claim, in three registers. <b>Green:</b> it printed recently — a fact. <b>Amber:</b> it has been silent and the last line looks like a question — stated as a guess, with the evidence attached. There is deliberately no third "it is waiting" state, because we would be asserting something we cannot know.</p></div>
<div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#fbf1dd;color:#8a5a00;font:600 10px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em">BEHAVIOUR CHANGE</span><p style="margin:6px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>Promote the last printed line.</b> A question is almost always the final non-empty line, and it is currently buried at the bottom of a scrolling <span style="font:11.5px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">&lt;pre&gt;</span> at 12px. Lifting it above the transcript, unwrapped and unedited, is a pure presentation move — no parsing, no interpretation, just "here is the tail".</p></div>
<div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#fbf1dd;color:#8a5a00;font:600 10px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em">BEHAVIOUR CHANGE</span><p style="margin:6px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty">Widen the silence trigger from 3s to <b>~10s, and show a counter</b>. Three seconds fires constantly during normal work, which trains people to ignore it. A visible "quiet for 14 seconds" degrades gracefully: at 4 minutes it reads as concerning without the UI ever having to decide it is.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>No suggested replies, no order/drop buttons.</b> Parsing <span style="font:11.5px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">[order/drop]</span> into two buttons would be the browser deciding what the agent accepts. The user types.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Amber surrounds the whole panel rather than one badge — this is the state where the poll must not steal focus or clear the draft, so the draft's persistence is stated on screen.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</sc-if>
</div>

<div id="a5" style="padding:24px 48px 12px;display:flex;gap:34px;align-items:flex-start;scroll-margin-top:16px">
<div style="flex:none;width:1180px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:0 0 12px;font:600 11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680"><span style="padding:3px 7px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff;border-radius:4px">05</span><span style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:#1c1b19">Plan review — human gate 1</span></div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px 0;font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;height:820px;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:12px;flex:none">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px"><span style="font:600 20px/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:-.01em">R3DA-13673</span><span style="font-size:13.5px;color:#6b6862">Column picker for All Facilities · frontend, all-facilities</span></div>
<a href="#" style="font-size:12.5px;text-decoration:none">Jira ↗</a>
</div>
<div style="flex:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px;padding:13px 16px;border:1px solid #d7e2fb;background:#f4f7fe;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:14px">
<span style="flex:none;font:14px/1.2 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#2563eb;margin-top:1px">◆</span>
<div style="flex:1">
<div style="font:600 13.5px/1.35 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">This story is stopped at plan review and only you can move it.</div>
<div style="font-size:12.5px;color:#3f3d39;margin-top:3px">It has been here since 09:14. There is no timeout and nothing happens if you leave — the plan is below, the decision is at the end of it.</div>
</div>
<a href="#a5" style="flex:none;align-self:center;padding:7px 12px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #c9d8f7;border-radius:8px;font:500 12.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#2563eb;text-decoration:none">Jump to the decision ↓</a>
</div>

<div style="flex:1;min-height:0;overflow:auto;padding-bottom:4px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:12px">
<div style="font:600 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Acceptance criteria · 5</div>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px"><span style="padding:3px 9px;border-radius:20px;background:#e8f4ec;color:#157f4a;font:500 11.5px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">every criterion quotes the ticket</span></div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea">
<div style="flex:none;width:34px;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">AC1</div>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:#1c1b19">Users can configure which columns they see in the All Facilities list view</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0 0;border-left:2px solid #e8e5e0;padding-left:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;font-style:italic">"users can configure what columns they want to see"</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-top:7px"><span style="padding:2px 7px;border-radius:5px;background:#f0eeea;font:11px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#3f3d39">frontend · opens picker, toggles visibility</span><span style="padding:2px 7px;border-radius:5px;background:#f0eeea;font:11px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#3f3d39">all-facilities · show and hide columns</span></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea">
<div style="flex:none;width:34px;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">AC2</div>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:#1c1b19">Re-ordering the columns is supported <span style="color:#8a5a00;font-size:12.5px">(the ticket calls this optional)</span></div>
<div style="margin:6px 0 0;border-left:2px solid #e8e5e0;padding-left:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;font-style:italic">"re-ordering the columns could be useful for visual comparisons"</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-top:7px"><span style="padding:2px 7px;border-radius:5px;background:#f0eeea;font:11px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#3f3d39">frontend · reorder by drag or menu</span></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea">
<div style="flex:none;width:34px;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">AC3</div>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:#1c1b19">The column configuration is saved and restored across reloads</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0 0;border-left:2px solid #e8e5e0;padding-left:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;font-style:italic">"saving that configuration might be useful for repeating tasks"</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-top:7px"><span style="padding:2px 7px;border-radius:5px;background:#f0eeea;font:11px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#3f3d39">frontend · persists across page reloads</span></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea">
<div style="flex:none;width:34px;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">AC4</div>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:#1c1b19">Every column available today stays selectable — none disappear from the picker</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0 0;border-left:2px solid #e8e5e0;padding-left:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;font-style:italic">"none of the current columns should disappear from the available columns for selection"</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;padding:11px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea">
<div style="flex:none;width:34px;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">AC5</div>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
<div style="font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:#1c1b19">A new Description column is added and appears in the picker</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0 0;border-left:2px solid #e8e5e0;padding-left:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;font-style:italic">"new column 'Description' should be added"</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:12px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #e8e5e0">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px"><span style="font:600 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Implementation plan</span><span style="font:11.5px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">specs/R3DA-13673/implementation-plan.md</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden;font:500 11.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif"><span style="padding:6px 11px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff">Reading</span><span style="padding:6px 11px;background:#fff;color:#6b6862">Source</span></div>
</div>
<div style="padding:16px 18px;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.65;color:#3f3d39;max-width:74ch">
<div style="font:600 14px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;margin-bottom:6px">Approach</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;text-wrap:pretty">Column visibility becomes a user-scoped preference stored alongside the existing saved-view record, so the All Facilities grid reads one settings object instead of two. The picker is a new panel in the existing grid toolbar rather than a modal, because reordering needs the grid visible behind it.</p>
<div style="font:600 14px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;margin:14px 0 6px">Work packages</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px">
<div style="display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 12px;background:#faf9f7;border-radius:8px"><span style="flex:none;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">WP1</span><div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#1c1b19">Column picker panel and visibility toggles</div><div style="font:11px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">frontend · AC1 AC2 AC4 AC5 · 4 test ids</div></div></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 12px;background:#faf9f7;border-radius:8px"><span style="flex:none;font:600 11.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">WP2</span><div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#1c1b19">Description column and preference persistence</div><div style="font:11px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#8a8680">all-facilities · AC3 AC5 · 3 test ids</div></div></div>
</div>
<div style="font:600 14px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;margin:14px 0 6px">Out of scope</div>
<p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Per-view column sets, and column widths. Neither is quoted in the ticket.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:flex;gap:14px">
<details style="flex:1;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px"><summary style="font:500 13px/1.4 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#2563eb;cursor:pointer">Ticket source — specs/R3DA-13673/jira-source.md</summary></details>
<div style="flex:none;width:300px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px">
<div style="font:600 11px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:8px">AIU CREDITS</div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:12px/1.9 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#3f3d39"><span>intake</span><span>0.4</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:12px/1.9 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#3f3d39"><span>planning</span><span>2.1</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:600 12px/1.9 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#1c1b19;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea;margin-top:4px;padding-top:4px"><span>so far</span><span>2.5</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #2563eb;border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px">
<div style="font:600 15px/1.3 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;margin-bottom:4px">Your decision on this plan</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:13px;color:#3f3d39;max-width:70ch;text-wrap:pretty">Approving sends the story to implementation across <span style="font:12px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">frontend</span> and <span style="font:12px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">all-facilities</span>. Leaving this page changes nothing.</p>
<textarea placeholder="A reason. Leave this empty to approve; write in it to send the plan back or reject the story." style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;height:74px;padding:11px 13px;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:8px;font:13.5px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;resize:vertical;background:#faf9f7"></textarea>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-top:12px">
<button style="padding:11px 20px;background:#157f4a;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:600 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Approve the plan</button>
<button style="padding:11px 18px;background:#f7f6f4;color:#a5a099;border:1px solid #eae7e2;border-radius:8px;font:500 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Send back</button>
<button style="padding:11px 18px;background:#f7f6f4;color:#a5a099;border:1px solid #eae7e2;border-radius:8px;font:500 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Reject</button>
<span style="font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;margin-left:4px">Send back and Reject need a reason in the box. Revisions used: 0 of 4.</span>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px">
<div style="font:600 11px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:10px">DECISION LOG</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;padding:5px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea"><span style="flex:none;width:112px">08:58</span><span style="flex:none;width:110px">intake</span><span>gate passed · exit 0</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;padding:5px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea"><span style="flex:none;width:112px">09:14</span><span style="flex:none;width:110px">planning</span><span>gate passed · exit 0 · handed to plan_review</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="flex:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:11px 16px;margin:0 -20px;background:#fff;border-top:1px solid #e8e5e0;box-shadow:0 -6px 18px rgba(28,27,25,.05)">
<span style="width:8px;height:8px;background:#2563eb;flex:none;transform:rotate(45deg)"></span>
<div style="flex:1;font-size:12.5px;color:#3f3d39"><b style="color:#1c1b19">Plan review</b> · waiting on you since 09:14 · no timeout, no default</div>
<a href="#a5" style="padding:7px 13px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d7dbe3;border-radius:8px;font:500 12.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#2563eb;text-decoration:none">Go to the decision ↓</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<sc-if value="{{ showNotes }}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
<div style="flex:none;width:320px;position:sticky;top:16px;font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="border-left:2px solid #cfcbc4;padding:2px 0 2px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:6px">BRIEF 3 · DECISION UNDER A LONG PAGE</div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The reading order is untouched: criteria, plan, packages, credits, <i>then</i> the decision, <i>then</i> the log. What is added is a <b>sticky rail that carries no verb</b> — it states the phase and how long it has waited, and offers a scroll link. You can always reach the decision in one click; you can never make it from the rail.</p></div>
<div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#fbf1dd;color:#8a5a00;font:600 10px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em">BEHAVIOUR CHANGE</span><p style="margin:6px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty">I considered a sticky Approve button and rejected it. A control that is permanently under the cursor is exactly the nudge the harness forbids — the scroll <i>is</i> the friction, and it is the good kind.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The <b>blue strip at the top</b> answers "why am I here" before any content, and repeats the two facts that matter most: nothing expires, nothing happens if you leave.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The decision panel is the only <b>2px border</b> in the product. Emphasis by weight, not by colour fill — a filled panel would read as an alert, and there is nothing wrong here.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>The box's placeholder teaches the arming rule</b> in one sentence, so the greyed Send back is explained before it is discovered. Disabled buttons stay visible rather than hidden: their existence is information.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Approve is green, not the accent blue. Blue is navigation and identity throughout; the two irreversible verbs get semantic colour so they never look like links.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</sc-if>
</div>

<div id="a6" style="padding:24px 48px 12px;display:flex;gap:34px;align-items:flex-start;scroll-margin-top:16px">
<div style="flex:none;width:1180px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;margin:0 0 12px;font:600 11px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680"><span style="padding:3px 7px;background:#1c1b19;color:#fff;border-radius:4px">06</span><span style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0;color:#1c1b19">Send back — reason typed, consequence stated, revision 4 of 4</span></div>
<div style="background:#faf9f7;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19">
<div style="background:#fff;border:2px solid #2563eb;border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px;max-width:840px">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:4px">
<div style="font:600 15px/1.3 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Your decision on this plan</div>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:12px;color:#8a5a00"><span>revisions</span><span style="display:inline-flex;gap:3px"><span style="width:9px;height:9px;background:#c98a00;border-radius:2px"></span><span style="width:9px;height:9px;background:#c98a00;border-radius:2px"></span><span style="width:9px;height:9px;background:#c98a00;border-radius:2px"></span><span style="width:9px;height:9px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #c98a00;border-radius:2px"></span></span><span style="font:600 12px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">3 of 4 used</span></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:13px;color:#3f3d39;max-width:70ch">You have written a reason, so Send back and Reject are armed and Approve is not.</p>
<textarea style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;height:82px;padding:11px 13px;border:1px solid #2563eb;border-radius:8px;font:13.5px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1c1b19;resize:vertical;background:#fff;outline:3px solid #dbe6fd">AC3 says the configuration is saved, but the plan stores it per user rather than per saved view. Every ticket in this epic has been per view. Re-plan AC3 against the saved-view record.</textarea>

<div style="margin-top:14px;border:1px solid #e8c98a;background:#fdfaf2;border-radius:9px;padding:14px 16px">
<div style="font:600 13px/1.35 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#8a5a00;margin-bottom:8px">If you send this back, three things happen</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="display:flex;gap:9px"><span style="flex:none;color:#c98a00">—</span><span>The approval you recorded at <span style="font:12px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">14:22 on 29 Aug</span> is cleared. This gate becomes undecided again.</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:9px"><span style="flex:none;color:#c98a00">—</span><span>The story returns to <span style="font:12px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">planning</span> and Cartographer re-plans with your text as its instruction.</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:9px"><span style="flex:none;color:#c98a00">—</span><span><b style="color:#8a5a00">This is the fourth and last revision.</b> After it, Send back is gone: the only ways out of this gate are approving the plan or starting the story over.</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-top:14px">
<button style="padding:11px 20px;background:#f7f6f4;color:#a5a099;border:1px solid #eae7e2;border-radius:8px;font:600 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif">Approve the plan</button>
<button style="padding:11px 18px;background:#8a5a00;color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:600 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Send back — last revision</button>
<button style="padding:11px 18px;background:#fff;color:#b4261a;border:1px solid #f2cdc8;border-radius:8px;font:500 13.5px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;cursor:pointer">Reject the story</button>
<span style="font-size:12.5px;color:#6b6862;margin-left:4px">Clear the box to approve instead.</span>
</div>
</div>

<div style="margin-top:18px;max-width:840px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e8e5e0;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px">
<div style="font:600 11px/1 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:10px">DECISION LOG</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;padding:5px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea"><span style="flex:none;width:112px">29 Aug 14:22</span><span style="flex:none;width:110px;color:#157f4a">approved</span><span>plan_review · no reason given</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;padding:5px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea"><span style="flex:none;width:112px">30 Aug 09:40</span><span style="flex:none;width:110px;color:#8a5a00">sent back</span><span>revision 2 · "criteria AC4 has no source quote"</span></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:14px;font:12px/1.7 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;color:#6b6862;padding:5px 0;border-top:1px solid #f0eeea"><span style="flex:none;width:112px">31 Aug 11:05</span><span style="flex:none;width:110px;color:#8a5a00">sent back</span><span>revision 3 · "split WP1, it spans two repos"</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<sc-if value="{{ showNotes }}" hint-placeholder-val="{{ true }}">
<div style="flex:none;width:320px;position:sticky;top:16px;font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#3f3d39">
<div style="border-left:2px solid #cfcbc4;padding:2px 0 2px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
<div><div style="font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8680;margin-bottom:6px">BRIEF 5 · CONSEQUENCES BEFORE THE CLICK</div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The consequence panel appears <b>as soon as the box has text</b>, between the box and the buttons, so it is physically in the path to the click. Not a confirm dialog: a dialog arrives after the decision is made and gets dismissed by reflex.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Three consequences, in the order they will happen, each naming the specific thing affected — the approval's actual timestamp, the actual phase it returns to. "This action cannot be undone" is the kind of sentence people have learned to skip.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty"><b>The ceiling is always visible</b>, as four pips, from revision zero. Learning about a limit at the moment it bites is the worst time to learn it. At 3 of 4 the button relabels itself — <i>Send back — last revision</i> — because that is the one number that changes what you would choose.</p></div>
<div><span style="display:inline-block;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#fbf1dd;color:#8a5a00;font:600 10px/1.6 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.06em">BEHAVIOUR CHANGE</span><p style="margin:6px 0 0;text-wrap:pretty">Send back takes amber rather than the neutral it has today, so the three verbs read as three different weights: green go, amber undo, red stop.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The <b>decision log quotes past reasons</b>. On the fourth revision the most useful thing on screen is what you already asked for three times.</p></div>
<div><p style="margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">The armed/unarmed pair is stated in words above the box as well as shown in the buttons — the rule is unusual enough that it should never have to be inferred from a grey fill.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</sc-if>
</div>

<div id="a7" style="padding:24px 48px 12px;display:flex;gap:34px;align-items:flex-start;scroll-margin-top:16px">
<div style="flex:none;width:1180px">
